      "message": "[warning] Line 74: 🟡 `notificationSystemConnection` decides fallback from a one-time snapshot of `callStatus`. If a subscriber starts while status is not ongoing (e.g., `RINGING`) and the call later transitions to `CURRENT` without Telecom attaching, this `Single` still waits on `systemConnectionSubject` and can keep the notification pipeline blocked. Build this as a reactive fallback that also listens for the call becoming ongoing (or re-evaluates on state transitions), so the stream can unblock when status changes.",
